      "body": "## Summary\n\nPreserve `tool_call_id` on incoming tool replies and expose it in the chat request schema. The field stays optional for existing clients.\n\n```diff\n class ChatMessage(BaseModel):\n     tool_calls: list[FunctionCall] | None = None\n+    tool_call_id: str | None = None\n```\n\nRefs #4881. This covers request parsing and schema metadata; inference continues to use the existing positional message history.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- **Before:** original-module regression tests: 4 failed, 6 passed; supplied IDs disappeared from message/request serialization and the request JSON schema.\n  **After:** 10 passed, including nested round-trip, schema exposure, omitted/null ID and existing tool-call controls.\n- Changed-file pre-commit checks, license check, and sdist/wheel build from the clean staged source pass.\n- Full suite attempted: offline run had 217 passed, 121 failed, 25 skipped, 7 xfailed and 9 errors with uncached model assets; after enabling the host SOCKS proxy dependency, a bounded online run reached 89 passed / 5 skipped before interruption during Qwen3-VL asset loading (478s; exit130). Full suite is not claimed passing.\n- Repository-wide `make quality` reports existing whitespace in `model/patcher.py`; the existing SUPA RMSNorm file also needs formatting. These unrelated files retain their original contents.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** two-way.\n\n**Blast Radius:** API. One optional request field; no storage migration.\n",
